percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduced in:\nv4.7.dev2.official [778cf54da]\nv4.6.2.rc1.official [257ac3532]\nv4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev2 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - GeForce GTX 550 Ti - Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-2100 CPU @ 3.10GHz (4 threads) - 11.95 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nA saved editor layout includes the selected file system folder, ex `abc`.\nLoading the editor layout, shows an error in projects without that folder.\nExample:\n>  ERROR: Cannot navigate to 'res://abc/' as it has not been found in the file system!\n\nWhen an editor layout is saved with the name: `a`\nThe file: `AppData\\Roaming\\Godot\\editor_layouts.cfg`\nHas a section: `[a/FileSystem]`\nWith the entry: `selected_paths=PackedStringArray(\"res://abc/\")`\n\nExpected:\nWhen an editor layout loads. Select the base folder: `res://`, if the saved folder doesn't exist.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- in an empty project\n- in the file system panel\n- add a folder, ex: `abc`\n- select it\n- in the top menu, choose: `Editor > Editor Layout > Save Layout...`\n- type a name, ex: `a`\n- press: `enter`\n- in the file system panel\n- delete the folder: `abc`\n- in the top menu, choose: `Editor > Editor Layout > a`\n\nIssue:\nThe output panel shows:\n>   ERROR: Cannot navigate to 'res://abc/' as it has not been found in the file system!\n\nExpected:\nSelect the base folder: `res://` since the saved folder `abc` doesn't exist.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A, it's reproducible in an empty project.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"